[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mBreaking Changes[22m[39m                                                                                                   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mAdded[22m[39m                                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mGPT-6 Astra ([38;5;109mgpt-6-astra[39m) is now a built-in recommended default model at thinking level [38;5;109mhigh[39m, placed ahead of        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   GPT-5.6 Sol which remains the OpenAI fallback recommendation.                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mPersistent monitors now survive repeated restarts: file watches are re-registered and compare their persisted        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   checkpoint once, reporting exactly one detached created, replaced, or modified change (and nothing when unchanged),  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   while command watches are re-run once under the same [38;5;109mmon_[39m id without replaying pre-restart output. Sessions may keep [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   up to five durable watches; each expires seven days after creation without extending that deadline on restart or     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   rearm, and a watch muted by the wake budget remains muted when restored.                                             [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mA standing watch that exceeds its 200-line matching-event budget within a rolling 24-hour window now mutes itself    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   and says so once, telling you to rearm it; rearming resumes the watch, ordinary one-shot monitors are never counted, [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   and the window survives restarts so a noisy watch cannot receive a fresh allowance.                                  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mFixed[22m[39m                                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mRestored the literal [38;5;109mWorking[39m text shimmer and formatter by removing duplicate working status indicator construction. [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFavorite-model cycling (Ctrl+P) no longer breaks callers that predate the skipped-model list, and it raises the      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   documented model-usability budget error again when the single alternative cannot host the current context instead of [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   silently staying on the current model.                                                                               [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mChanged[22m[39m                                                                                                            [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mThe GPT-6 Astra prompt preset names the subscription form an eval session can call ([38;5;109mtool.monitor(...)[39m from the cell  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   that starts the run) instead of gating the rule on a [38;5;109mmonitor[39m tool the session withholds, lists the conditions worth  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   a watch, and arms one the moment the user names such state, so a CI run, PR, deploy, or long command is subscribed   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   to without being asked instead of polled.                                                                            [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mThe GPT-6 Astra prompt preset now treats the asynchronous form as the default for every call that offers one (child  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   tasks and bash sessions start in the background, long eval cells detach) and names the only two cases for blocking,  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   so a single dependent delegation is spawned in the background and the turn ends to wait instead of blocking on it.   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mThe [38;5;109mmonitor[39m tool's [38;5;109mpersistent[39m option now reads as what it is — a standing watch: no deadline, survives a session     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   restart (the command is re-run once, the file is rescanned and any change missed while detached is reported),        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   expires seven days after creation, and at most five per session. The native file branch no longer claims to reject   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;109mpersistent[39m, since a persistent file watch is exactly the one that is checkpointed and restored, and the guidance the [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   tool description duplicated from the terminal prompt section was removed rather than restated, so the reworded       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   switch and its bounds cost fewer prompt bytes than the wording they replace.                                         [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mFixed[22m[39m                                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mStarting a session with a compatible [38;5;109m-fast[39m catalog variant now keeps fast mode enabled and preserves the requested   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   thinking level when the variant is normalized to its base model; remembered service-tier behavior for ordinary       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   base-model starts is unchanged.                                                                                      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mInteractive shared-host regression tests now wait for RPC child processes to exit before removing their temporary    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   roots, preventing teardown [38;5;109mENOTEMPTY[39m races.                                                                          [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mMake the reftable polling fallback detect content changes without relying on filesystem timestamp precision, and     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   test the fallback with deterministic timer/event control.                                                            [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mRemoved[22m[39m                                                                                                            [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m[2026.9.4-3] - 2026-09-04[22m[39m                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mBreaking Changes[22m[39m                                                                                                   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mAdded[22m[39m                                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mTerminal monitors and background Bash sessions are now recorded per session, and a fresh startup reports what was    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   carried over, lost, expired, or unreadable in exactly one notification instead of silently dropping the state;       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   durable watches are reported as lost rather than resumed for now, while reloads continue preserving live terminal    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   state without this report.                                                                                           [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mChanged[22m[39m                                                                                                            [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mTerminal monitors now expose a stable [38;5;109mmon_[39m id in their result while retaining the runtime [38;5;109mbash_N[39m handle as           [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;109mdetails.bash_id[39m, and [38;5;109mbash_output[39m, [38;5;109mbash_input[39m, [38;5;109mbash_resize[39m, [38;5;109mkill_bash[39m, and monitor rearming accept either id.         [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;222m[1m### [22m[39m[38;5;222m[1mFixed[22m[39m                                                                                                              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mA clean checkout no longer fails [38;5;109mbun install --frozen-lockfile[39m, because the committed lockfile now matches the       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;109m@anthropic-ai/sdk[39m override in [38;5;109mpackage.json[39m.                                                                          [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mA spawned RPC host that never answers [38;5;109mget_protocol_info[39m now reports why. Its teardown validated pid ownership with a [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   process-identity probe that throws when the platform query fails (on Windows a starved [38;5;109mpowershell.exe[39m CIM read), so  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   the failure surfaced as [38;5;109mCommand failed: powershell.exe …[39m instead of the readiness diagnostic and the pidfile and     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   socket were left behind. A just-spawned host is now stopped through its own process handle, a probe that fails       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   against a live pid is retried and then reported as a typed unreadable-identity error instead of the raw shell        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   failure, and a probe that fails against a dead pid simply reads as gone — so the same Windows probe flake can no     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   longer surface from concurrent starts, attach, or teardown.                                                          [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFixed Anthropic native tool search sending [38;5;109mtool_reference[39m blocks under a [38;5;109mname[39m field instead of the API's [38;5;109mtool_name[39m,  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   and restricted the injected BM25 server tool to models that actually support tool search (Opus/Sonnet 4.5+ and       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   Fable), so Anthropic-compatible gateways and proxies no longer 400 and permanently fall back to local [38;5;109mtool_search[39m    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   for the session.                                                                                                     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mImage generation no longer fails with an OpenAI 401 when a placeholder API key is stored for the [38;5;109mopenai[39m provider. A  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   seeded [38;5;109mSK-SENTINEL-DO-NOT-LOG[39m value is treated as absent instead of as a credential, so resolution falls through to  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   a configured OpenAI-compatible gateway, and image generation is reported as not configured when no gateway exists.   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mHook trust-state reads no longer fail tool execution when the lock directory cannot be created ([38;5;109mEPERM[39m/[38;5;109mEACCES[39m/[38;5;109mEROFS[39m   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   in sandboxed or read-only children); writers still fail closed on those errors.                                      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFile-backed credential, auth, and settings locks now wait through bounded contention retries; exhausted waits report [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   an actionable transient [38;5;109mCredentialStoreBusyError[39m instead of burning the provider fallback chain.                     [0m]8;;
