[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFixed queued steering and follow-up messages still reaching the provider after a queue clear on a terminating        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   continuation: the terminating continuation boundary now runs before the drained queue is refreshed, so a clear or    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   replacement at [38;5;109mturn_start[39m wins over pending input.                                                                   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFixed [38;5;109mprepareNextTurn[39m and [38;5;109mprepareNextTurnWithContext[39m being skipped on completed turns without tool calls: the        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   next-turn preparation now runs after every completed assistant turn that can reach the preparation boundary,         [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   including a normal stop response, while the terminating queue boundary and ownership refresh are preserved before a  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   continuation provider request.                                                                                       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mFixed next-turn compaction firing on completed turns that will not reach the provider: compaction is now gated on    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   real provider admission (a tool continuation or queued message actually being admitted), while the next-turn         [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   callback keeps running on every completed turn and the late queue re-sample and one bounded callback replay after    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   compaction are retained.                                                                                             [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mErrored and aborted provider turns are now excluded from every LLM request at the session level: [38;5;109mconvertToLlm[39m runs   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   the shared [38;5;109mdropFailedAssistantTurns[39m from [38;5;109m@earendil-works/pi-ai[39m as its final step, so lanes that build requests       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   straight from its output (the claude-sdk-oauth prompt bridge's [38;5;109m<conversation_history>[39m rendering and cursor turn      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   building) no longer replay a failed turn's partial text and unexecuted tool calls, and token estimation              [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   ([38;5;109mestimateContextTokens(buildSessionContext(...))[39m) no longer counts them. A tool call id re-declared by a later kept  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   assistant keeps its result; [38;5;109mstop[39m/[38;5;109mlength[39m/[38;5;109mtoolUse[39m turns are untouched; the provider transform layer's existing drop in [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;109mtransform-messages.ts[39m stays as-is.                                                                                   [0m]8;;
