[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mClaude SDK OAuth restart continuity now persists from the compaction-aware active context, survives                  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   goal-continuation metadata and a resident entry closing before [38;5;109mmessage_end[39m, and therefore avoids flattening and      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   re-sending an oversized full transcript after restart.                                                               [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mMulti-session RPC socket clients no longer lose assistant text when they fall behind: a queued [38;5;109mmessage_update[39m        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   snapshot superseded by a newer one is now delivered in its delta-only form instead of being replaced, so [38;5;109mtext_delta[39m  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   streams stay lossless the way the stdout path already was. A stalled omo-desktop reader had lost a 411-character     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   window and rendered a message that started mid-word.                                                                 [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mA multi-session RPC socket whose per-connection event queue overflows is now closed (after the [38;5;109moverflow[39m record),     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   instead of being left open while the host silently dropped every later record and command response for it; the       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   client reconnects and resyncs. The overflow is reported to stderr with the queued/incoming/max byte counts and a     [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   preview of the offending record, and the default per-connection cap rises from 4 MiB to 64 MiB, which four inline    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   image tool results had exceeded in one burst.                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39m[38;5;109m/gpt-account remove[39m (and every other account-removal path) now leaves the remaining account actually in use.         [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   Removing the account the stored credential's top-level fields projected used to keep those fields pointing at the    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   deleted account's tokens, and a provider left with one account does not enter credential rotation, so requests kept  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   authenticating as the removed account; the surviving account's material is now projected onto those fields.          [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mClaude SDK OAuth classifies Fable-style "requires usage credits" failures as a non-retryable entitlement instead of  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   a rate limit, so the account is not blocked for 60s and AgentSession can fall through to the next model ([38;5;109m[4m#709[24m[39m[38;5;241m        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;241m(https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/issues/709)[39m).                                                                 [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mPrint mode ([38;5;109m-p[39m / [38;5;109m--mode json[39m) now writes a stderr notice when retry fallback substitutes a model, so silent          [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   wrong-model answers are visible without corrupting JSON stdout ([38;5;109m[4moh-my-openagent#7626[24m[39m[38;5;241m                                 [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;241m(https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/7626)[39m).                                                      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mClaude SDK OAuth host-tool denial now states that Senpi executes the tool on the host and returns the result as the  [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   next user message, so models no longer treat "Do not retry with other tools; end the turn." as a failure ([38;5;109m[4m#784[24m[39m[38;5;241m       [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;241m(https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/issues/784)[39m, [38;5;109m[4moh-my-openagent#7115[24m[39m[38;5;241m                                             [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;241m(https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/7115)[39m).                                                      [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;                                                                                                                        [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;; [38;5;109m- [39mClaude SDK OAuth no longer falls back to the host [38;5;109mclaude[39m CLI login when a managed lane is selected and its account   [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   pool is empty: [38;5;109moauth-slots[39m and [38;5;109mconfig-dir[39m now fail with [38;5;109mNo Claude SDK OAuth accounts configured for the managed lane [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   [38;5;109m[39m instead of silently answering with ambient credentials after [38;5;109m/logout[39m. The ambient lane (no [38;5;109mtokenInjection[39m and no    [0m]8;;
[2K[0m]8;;   stored accounts) is unchanged.                                                                                       [0m]8;;
